hadiths[122]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2899","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform Hajj and Umrah one after the other (in succession), for performing them consecutively removes poverty and sins just as the furnace removes the impurities of iron."
"2900","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform Hajj and Umrah one after the other (in succession), for these two remove sins just as the furnace removes the impurities of iron."
"2901","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform Hajj and Umrah one after the other (in succession), for these two remove poverty, neediness and sins just as the furnace removes the impurities of iron, gold and silver; and there is no reward for an accepted Hajj (Hajj mabrur) except Paradise."
"2902","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, camels will come to their owner in their best and fattest condition; if he had not paid Allah's right on them (zakah), they will trample him with their feet. And sheep and goats will come to their owner in their best condition; if he had not paid their right, they will trample him with their hooves and butt him with their horns. And one of their rights is that they be milked at the watering place. Beware! Let none of you come on the Day of Resurrection carrying on his neck a camel that is groaning, and call out to me: 'O Muhammad!' For I will answer him: 'I have no power to do anything for you; I had conveyed the message.' Beware! Let none of you come on the Day of Resurrection carrying on his neck a goat that is bleating, and call out to me: 'O Muhammad!' For I will answer him: 'I have no power to do anything for you; I had conveyed the message.' And the treasure of any one of you (who did not pay zakah) will become, on the Day of Resurrection, a bald venomous snake; its owner will flee from it, and the snake will pursue him, saying: 'I am your treasure.' It will keep pursuing him until that person puts his fingers into its mouth."
"2903","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let one of you (women, for the ritual bath after menstruation) take her water and lote-tree leaves and purify herself thoroughly well, then pour water over her head and rub it vigorously until the water reaches the roots of the hair on her head (and its partings), then pour water over herself, then take a piece of cotton or cloth scented with musk and purify herself with it (by cleaning the place of the blood)."
"2904","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The charities of the Muslims (that is, the zakah on livestock) are to be collected at their springs and watering places (where they come to drink water)."
"2905","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The fire of Hell will burn the whole body of the son of Adam except the marks of prostration, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden the Fire to burn the marks of prostration."
"2906","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trade gold for silver however you wish, and trade silver for gold however you wish (that is, if it is hand to hand, it is permissible with an increase or decrease)."
"2907","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ruin (and destruction) be to gold and silver."
"2908","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your smiling in the face of your Muslim brother is charity for you; your enjoining good and forbidding evil is charity; your showing the way to a person who has gone astray is charity for you; your removing a stone, a thorn and a bone from the road is charity for you; and your pouring water from your bucket into your brother's bucket is also charity for you."
"2909","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On Friday, the angels are sent to the doors of the mosque; they write down the name of the first to arrive, then the one who comes after him. Then when the imam ascends the pulpit, the scrolls (of deeds) are rolled up."
"2910","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever spat in the direction of the Qiblah, on the Day of Resurrection that phlegm (or spittle) of his will be brought in such a state that it is stuck on his face."
"2911","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The ornament of the believer (in Paradise) will reach as far as the water of his ablution reaches."
"2912","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The dwellings (of Madinah) will (spread out and) reach the place called Ihab."
"2913","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will leave Madinah in its best condition; only birds and beasts of prey will (come and) dwell in it. And the last to be gathered will be two shepherds from the tribe of Muzaynah who will want to come to Madinah; they will come driving their goats, and they will find them in the form of wild animals. Until, when they reach Thaniyyat al-Wada' (the mountain pass), they will fall on their faces (that is, they will die)."
"2914","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Overlook punishing noble and dignified people for their (minor) slips."
"2915","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(The prayer of) Friday is obligatory upon every Muslim, except a woman, a child or a slave."
"2916","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will find people like mines (of minerals); those of them who were best in the time of ignorance (Jahiliyyah) are also the best after accepting Islam, provided they gain understanding of the religion. And you will find the best person in this matter (of authority and leadership) to be the one who most detested it before falling into that office. And you will find the worst person with Allah on the Day of Resurrection to be the one who is two-faced: (that is, the one who comes to one group with one face and to another with another face)."
"2917","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep the prayer light, for behind you there are the weak, the elderly and the one who has a need."
"2918","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before the Hour, a wind will blow in which the soul of every believer will be taken."
"2919","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Paradise and Hell disputed with each other. Hell said: 'I have been singled out for the arrogant and the tyrants.' And Paradise said: 'What is the matter with me that none enter me except the weak, the lowly and the helpless among people?' So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said to Paradise: 'You are My mercy; through you I show mercy to whomever I wish among My servants.' And He said to Hell: 'You are My punishment; through you I punish whomever I wish among My servants. And each of you shall be filled.' As for Hell, it will not be filled until Allah places His foot upon it; then it will say: 'Enough, enough!' Then it will be filled, and its parts will draw together into one another, and Allah does not wrong anyone of His creation. As for Paradise, Allah will bring into being a new creation for it."
"2920","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr), and whoever wishes to seek it, let him seek it on the twenty-seventh night."
"2921","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr) in the last seven nights of Ramadan."
"2922","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr) in the odd nights of the last ten days of Ramadan."
"2923","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr) on the twenty-third night."
"2924","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will be raised barefoot, naked and uncircumcised, in the same state in which you were born."
"2925","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Move into the shade."
"2926","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Move away from this place of yours in which heedlessness overtook you."
"2927","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Beast (Dabbat al-Ard) will emerge from the earth and will put a mark on people's noses; then they will live long lives among you, until a man will buy an animal and will be asked: 'From whom did you buy it?' And he will say: 'From the man whose nose is marked.'"
"2928","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Choose well for your offspring; so marry those who are your equals, and marry your daughters to them."
"2929","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Treat illness with cow's milk, for I hope that Allah has placed a cure in it, because the cow eats from every kind of tree and plant."
"2930","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O servants of Allah! Seek treatment, for Allah Almighty has not created any disease without placing a remedy for it, except one disease: old age."
"2931","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The eye sheds tears and the heart grieves, but we will say only what pleases the Lord. By Allah! O Ibrahim, we are grieved by your parting."
"2932","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The eye sheds tears and the heart grieves, and we do not say what angers the Lord. Were it not that this is a true promise and a place of gathering, and that the later of us will join the earlier, we would grieve for you, O Ibrahim, far more than we have grieved; and indeed we are grieved by your parting, O Ibrahim."
"2933","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the sun will come so close to the people that it will be at a distance of only one mile from them, and the people will be in sweat according to their deeds: some up to their ankles, some up to their knees, some up to their waists, and some whom the sweat will bridle like a rein."
"2934","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The mill of Islam will keep turning for thirty-five, thirty-six or thirty-seven years. If they perish, then it is the path of those who perished; and if their religion remains established for them, it will remain established for seventy years, including the time that has already passed."
"2935","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The good people among you will pass away one after another, until none of you remain except as few as these."
"2936","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Ummah will come to me at the Pond (Hawd), and I will drive people away from it as a man drives other people's camels away from his own camels. The Companions said: 'O Prophet of Allah! Will you recognise us?' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Yes, you will have a mark that no one other than you will have; you will come to me with radiant foreheads, hands and feet from the traces of ablution. But a group of you will certainly be turned away from me, and they will not be able to reach me. So I will say: ""O my Lord! These are my companions!"" Then an angel will answer me and say: ""Do you know what new things they invented after you?""'"
"2937","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have left among you two things, after which you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my Sunnah, and these two will never separate until they come to me at the Pond (Hawd)."
"2938","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Marry, even if the dowry (mahr) is only an iron ring."
"2939","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Marry virgins, for they are sweeter of tongue, more fertile of womb, and more content with little."
"2940","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Marry women who are loving and bear many children, for I will take pride in your great numbers before the other nations."
"2941","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Marry, for I will take pride in you before the other nations, and do not be like the monasticism of the Christians."
"2942","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An orphan girl is to be asked for her permission regarding her marriage; if she remains silent, that is her permission, and if she refuses, there is no compulsion upon her."
"2943","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat the pre-dawn meal (suhur), for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal."
"2944","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat the pre-dawn meal (suhur), even if it is only with water."
"2945","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat the pre-dawn meal (suhur), even if it is only a sip of water."
"2946","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Giving the greeting of salam by pointing with one finger is the way of the Jews."
"2947","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will hear hadith, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who heard it from you."
"2948","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah."
"2949","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Name yourselves with my name but do not take my kunyah, for I am Abu al-Qasim; I distribute among you."
"2950","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give charity, for a time will come upon you when a man will go about with his charity, and the one to whom he takes it will say: 'Had you brought it yesterday, I would have accepted it, but now I have no need of it.' So he will find no one to accept it."
"2951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give charity, even if it is only a single date, for it relieves the hunger of the hungry and extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire."
"2952","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spend, and do not hoard your wealth, or else provision will be withheld from you as well."
"2953","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's voluntary prayer in his home is superior to his voluntary prayer in front of people, just as a man's prayer in congregation is superior to his prayer alone."
"2954","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pardon the prescribed punishments (hudud) among yourselves, for whatever prescribed punishment reaches me becomes binding."
"2955","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Come, pledge allegiance to me on the condition that you will not associate anything with Allah, you will not steal, you will not commit adultery, you will not kill your children, you will not bring forth a slander that you have fabricated between your hands and your feet, and you will not disobey me in anything good. Whoever among you fulfils this, his reward is with Allah; whoever commits any of these and is punished for it in this world, that will be an expiation for him; and whoever commits any of these and Allah conceals it, his matter rests with Allah: if He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will pardon him."
"2956","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep up your commitment to the Qur'an, for by the One in whose Hand is my soul, it escapes from the hearts of men faster than a camel escapes from its tether."
"2957","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasten to perform Hajj, for none of you knows what may befall him."
"2958","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The deeds of people are presented twice every week: on Monday and on Thursday. Then every believing servant is forgiven, except a servant between whom and his brother there is enmity, and it is said: 'Leave these two until they reconcile.'"
"2959","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday, and I love that my deeds be presented while I am fasting."
"2960","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trials are presented to hearts the way a mat is woven, reed by reed. Any heart that absorbs them has a black spot put in it, and any heart that rejects them has a white spot put in it, until one heart becomes white like a smooth stone, which no trial will harm as long as the heavens and the earth endure, and the other becomes black and dust-coloured like an overturned jug; it neither recognises any good nor rejects any evil, except what its desires have soaked into it."
"2961","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Know Allah in times of ease, and He will know you in times of hardship."
"2962","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May the slave of the dinar, the slave of the dirham and the slave of the striped cloak perish! If he is given, he is pleased, and if he is not given, he is displeased. May he perish and fall on his face, and if he is pricked by a thorn, may he find no one to remove it. Glad tidings for the servant who holds the rein of his horse in the path of Allah, his hair dishevelled and his feet covered in dust. If he is on guard duty, he stays on guard duty, and if he is in the rear of the army, he stays there. If he asks permission, it is not granted to him, and if he intercedes, his intercession is not accepted."
"2963","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Know that none of you will see his Lord until he dies."
"2964","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Learn the Book of Allah, keep up your commitment to it, and recite it in a beautiful voice, for by the One in whose Hand is my soul, it escapes faster than a pregnant she-camel escapes from its tether."
"2965","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Learn enough of your lineages to maintain your ties of kinship, for maintaining ties of kinship is a cause of love within the family, a means of increase in wealth and a source of blessing in one's lifespan."
"2966","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Learn from Quraysh and do not teach them; put Quraysh forward and do not hold them back, for a man of Quraysh has the strength of two men from other than Quraysh."
"2967","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from a bad neighbour in a place of permanent residence, for a temporary neighbour moves away from you."
"2968","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from severe trial, from the depth of misery, from an evil decree and from the gloating of enemies."
"2969","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will fight the Arabian Peninsula and Allah will grant you its conquest, then Persia and Allah will grant you its conquest, then you will fight the Romans and Allah will grant you its conquest, then you will fight the Dajjal and Allah will grant you victory over him."
"2970","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and on Thursday, and every servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except a man between whom and his brother there is enmity, and it is said: 'Wait for these two until they reconcile.'"
"2971","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The gates of the heaven are opened at midnight, and a caller calls out: 'Is there anyone supplicating, that he may be answered? Is there anyone asking, that he may be given? Is there anyone in distress, that his distress may be relieved?' So there remains no Muslim who makes a supplication except that Allah Almighty answers him, except an adulteress who earns through her private parts, or a tax collector."
"2972","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yemen will be conquered, and some people will come driving their mounts and move away with their families and those who obey them, while Madinah would be better for them if only they knew. And Syria will be conquered, and some people will come driving their mounts and move away with their families and those who obey them, while Madinah would be better for them if only they knew. And Iraq will be conquered, and some people will come driving their mounts and move away with their families and those who obey them, while Madinah would be better for them if only they knew."
"2973","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gog and Magog will be released, and they will come out upon the people, as Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: 'They will come swarming down from every elevation.' They will overwhelm the people, and the Muslims will withdraw from them into their cities and fortresses, gathering their livestock in with them. They will drink up the waters of the earth, until one of them will pass by a river and drink all that is in it, leaving it dry, so that whoever passes by that river after them will say: 'There used to be water here once.' When none of the people remain except the odd one in a fortress or a city, their leader will say: 'These were the people of the earth, and we have finished with them; now the people of the heaven remain!' Then one of them will brandish his spear and hurl it towards the sky, and it will return to him stained with blood; this will be a trial and a tribulation. While they are in this state, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will send worms into their necks like the worms that grow in the necks of locusts, and by morning they will be dead, with not a sound heard from them. The Muslims will say: 'Is there not a man who will sell his life for us and see what this enemy has done?' So a man among them will go out seeking reward, considering himself as good as killed, and he will go down and find them dead, piled one upon another. Then he will call out: 'O Muslims, rejoice! Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has sufficed you against your enemy.' Then they will come out of their cities and fortresses and let their livestock loose, and there will be no pasture for them except their flesh, and they will grow as fat from it as they ever grew from any vegetation."
"2974","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer in congregation surpasses the prayer of any of you alone by twenty-five degrees, and the angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the Fajr prayer."
"2975","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Reflect upon the blessings of Allah, and do not reflect upon the essence of Allah."
"2976","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Reflect upon the creation of Allah, and do not reflect upon the essence of Allah."
"2977","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will fight the Jews and prevail over them, until one of them hides behind a stone and the stone says: 'O servant of Allah, there is a Jew behind me, so kill him.'"
"2978","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guarantee me six things and I will guarantee you Paradise: when any of you speaks, let him not lie; when he makes a promise, let him not break it; when he is entrusted with something, let him not betray the trust; lower your gazes, restrain your hands and guard your private parts."
"2979","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ammar will be killed by the rebellious group."
"2980","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Come forward and follow me, and let those who come after you follow you. People will keep holding back until Allah holds them back."
"2981","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The hand is to be cut off for theft of the value of a shield."
"2982","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The thief's hand is to be cut off for theft of a quarter of a dinar or more."
"2983","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On Friday the angels sit at the doors of the mosques and record the first, the second and the third to arrive, until, when the imam comes out, the registers are rolled up."
"2984","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will be established while the Romans are the most numerous of people."
"2985","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has guaranteed, for the one who strives in His path, whom nothing brings out of his home except striving in Allah's path and affirming the truth of His words, that He will admit him into Paradise, or return him, with the reward and spoils he has gained, to the very home from which he set out."
"2986","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The expiation for every quarrel is two rak'ahs of prayer."
"2987","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be camels that are the devils' share and houses that are the devils' share."
"2988","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection the earth will be like a single loaf of bread, which the Compeller (Allah Almighty) will turn over with His Hand just as one of you turns over his bread on a journey; it will be a feast of hospitality for the people of Paradise."
"2989","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Souls will be in the form of birds clinging to the trees, until, when the Day of Resurrection comes, every soul will enter its body."
"2990","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be rulers who will say whatever they wish and no one will answer them back; they will fall headlong into the Fire, one after another."
"2991","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be a truce between you and Banu al-Asfar (the Romans), then they will betray you and march against you under eighty banners, with twelve thousand soldiers under every banner."
"2992","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before the Hour there will be days in which knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will descend and harj will increase; and harj means killing."
"2993","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Before the Hour there will be trials like pieces of a dark night. A man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever by evening, and a believer in the evening and a disbeliever by morning. People will sell their religion for a little of the goods of this world."
"2994","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be callers at the gates of Hell; whoever answers their call, they will throw him into it. They will be people of our own kind, speaking our own language. So hold fast to the community of the Muslims and their imam, and if there is neither a community nor an imam, then keep away from all those factions, even if you have to bite on the root of a tree until death overtakes you while you are in that state."
"2995","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be a truce, but with rancour in hearts that will not return to what they were. Then there will arise callers to misguidance. If on that day you find Allah's caliph on the earth, then hold fast to him, even if he wears your body out and takes your wealth; and if you do not find him, then set out into the land, even if you die while biting on the stump of a tree."
"2996","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The earth will cast out the treasures within it like pillars of gold and silver. The killer will come and say: 'It was for this that I killed.' The one who severed ties of kinship will come and say: 'It was for this that I severed my ties of kinship.' The thief will come and say: 'It was for this that my hand was cut off.' Then they will all leave it and will not take anything from it."
"2997","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""At a time of division among the Muslims, a rebellious group will break away, and whichever of the two groups is closer to the truth will fight them."
"2998","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Purify yourselves with the earth, for it is kind and gracious towards you."
"2999","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rinse your mouths and draw water into your noses, and the two ears are part of the head."
"3000","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep."
"3001","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Help descends from the sky in proportion to the expense, and patience descends in proportion to the calamity."
"3002","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guard yourselves against urine, for most of the punishment of the grave is because of it."
"3003","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman is married for four reasons: for her wealth, for her lineage, for her beauty, and for her religion. So win the one who is religious, may your hands be covered in dust."
"3004","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give gifts to one another, and you will come to love one another."
"3005","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Repent to Allah Almighty, for I repent to Him a hundred times every day."
"3006","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform ablution after eating camel meat, and do not perform ablution after eating the meat of sheep and goats. Pray in the pens of sheep and goats, and do not pray in the resting places of camels."
"3007","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform ablution after eating whatever has been touched by fire."
"3008","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who repents from sin is like one who has committed no sin at all."
"3009","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Being calm and deliberate is good in every matter except in the deeds of the Hereafter."
"3010","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Calmness and deliberation, moderation, and good conduct are one part of the twenty-four parts of prophethood."
"3011","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Calmness and patience are from Allah, and haste is from Satan."
"3012","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yawning in prayer is from Satan. So when one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can."
"3013","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yawning is from Satan. So when one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can, for when one of you says 'Ha' while yawning, Satan laughs at him."
"3014","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Speaking of the blessing of Allah is gratitude, and concealing it is ingratitude. Whoever is not grateful for a little is not grateful for much, and whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah. Unity is a blessing, and division is a punishment."
"3015","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Saying Subhan Allah is for men, and clapping is for women."
"3016","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is to cover it up."
"3017","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the Eid al-Fitr prayer, the takbirs are seven in the first rak'ah and five in the second, and the recitation is to be done after the takbirs in both rak'ahs."
"3018","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Talbinah (barley porridge) brings refreshment to the heart of the sick person and removes some of his grief."
"3019","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley and salt for salt must be like for like and hand to hand. Whoever gives more or asks for more has engaged in usury (riba), unless their kinds are different."
"3020","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tayammum is one strike for the face and one strike for the palms."
